Issue #378 plan review — DONE

**Web check:** This uses known Android building blocks, but I found no canonical “DUMP-only adb ZIP provider” recipe. AOSP defines `DUMP` as `signature|privileged|development`; its [permission guidance](https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/refs/heads/main/core/java/android/permission/Permissions.md) says an ordinary app can receive a lasting development-permission grant through `adb pm grant`. Android’s [`ContentProvider.call` documentation](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/content/ContentProvider) confirms the plan’s explicit permission check is necessary. AOSP’s [`content read` command](https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/android-vts-9.0_r17/cmds/content/src/com/android/commands/content/Content.java) copies file-descriptor bytes to stdout; `adb exec-out` is suitable for binary output.

**BLOCKING, access boundary:** [D10, line 138](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/docs/feature-requests/issue-378-2026-09-27-dev-app-local-log.md:138) says only the adb shell can use the door. A privileged app, or an ordinary app previously granted `DUMP` through adb, could read content and change switches. Add verbatim: “Keep the manifest DUMP permissions, and also require `Binder.getCallingUid() == Process.SHELL_UID` in every `openFile` and `call` entry before reading or changing state. Reject every other UID with `SecurityException`, including an app explicitly granted DUMP. Accept only the two named read-only URIs, mode `r`, and the three named call methods. Test a second app after granting it DUMP through adb.” [`SHELL_UID` is public API](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/os/Process).

**BLOCKING, ZIP delivery:** [D10, lines 139–140](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/docs/feature-requests/issue-378-2026-09-27-dev-app-local-log.md:139) combines a pipe with a binder thread waiting for the worker. If that wait includes writing the ZIP, the pipe fills before `openFile` returns its read end, so `content read` cannot drain it. A pipe has backpressure, not a ZIP-sized buffer; Android also warns its [pipe writer can block on a slow reader](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/content/ContentProvider.PipeDataWriter). Add verbatim: “Build each ZIP to a unique cache file on its existing worker. `openFile` waits only for that file to finish, with a stated timeout, then returns a read-only `ParcelFileDescriptor` for the completed file; it never waits for a pipe writer. On timeout or failure, return an error and remove partial output. The recording ZIP is built on the `CapturedAudioFiles` worker.” A file descriptor avoids a Binder ZIP-size limit.

**BLOCKING, cold start ordering:** A provider request can start main. Android [installs providers before calling `Application.onCreate`](https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/refs/heads/android13-s3-release/core/java/android/app/ActivityThread.java); this app’s current startup is in `ModelBootstrapApplication.kt:89–98`. A setter could reach the switch worker before D2 queues cold-start mirror repair, allowing repair to overtake the requested state. Add verbatim: “Provider methods wait, with a bound, for main `Application.onCreate` to queue and finish cold-start switch repair before submitting a setter or reading settled status. Initialize the readiness signal before provider publication; do no waiting in provider `onCreate`. A timeout returns Pending or an error without changing a switch. Test a cold provider launch with a mismatched DataStore value and flag, then a setter; the setter must be the last action.”

**NON-BLOCKING, Mac receipt:** The cited harness’s `_run` and `_adb_host` decode output as text (`wispr_eyes.py:412–414, 2730–2735`). Add verbatim: “Pull ZIPs through a separate binary `adb exec-out` path. Write to a temporary Mac file, check the command result and ZIP integrity including `device.txt`, then rename it; never pass ZIP bytes through the text adb helpers.”

Axes searched: DUMP grant **found**; `call` bypass **found and handled**; raw binary read **found**; pipe wait risk **found**; provider startup race **found**; D2/D6/D9 worker separation defect **not found**. S26 release-build door behavior remains **NOT VERIFIED**.

